        "pl-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "96f86e0e-6857-3e23-8d8e-268e37c47536",
                "word": "kontinuum",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "pl",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d040d7c7-4b60-37db-82de-74fe87571bd4",
                        "entry_id": "96f86e0e-6857-3e23-8d8e-268e37c47536",
                        "glosses": [
                            "ciągły, zgodny z porządkiem zbiór elementów, które przechodzą jeden w drugi"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a73ff0dd-3d46-41ee-b44a-9b3b14c9df46",
                                "sense_id": "d040d7c7-4b60-37db-82de-74fe87571bd4",
                                "text": "Potrzebujemy widzialnej przeszłości, widzialnego kontinuum, widzialnego mitu początków, upewniającego nas co do naszego kresu"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "54344825-7240-3e16-aecb-535d14e66f70",
                        "entry_id": "96f86e0e-6857-3e23-8d8e-268e37c47536",
                        "glosses": [
                            "moc zbioru liczb rzeczywistych"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.2\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "28c64b30-eb23-4007-8054-cfdbb4049cc9",
                        "source_entry_id": "96f86e0e-6857-3e23-8d8e-268e37c47536",
                        "source_sense_id": "d040d7c7-4b60-37db-82de-74fe87571bd4",
                        "target_lang_word": "continuum",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "continuum",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ac90fa31-b945-36bd-8c65-54a883434950",
                                        "entry_id": "2bb1eeb7-75ce-3870-b964-532097bdd2cc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A continuous series or whole, no part of which is noticeably different from its adjacent parts, although the ends or extremes of it are very different from each other."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6ae957a5-3a09-42c6-91e0-74c3626c62f0",
                                                "sense_id": "ac90fa31-b945-36bd-8c65-54a883434950",
                                                "text": "Near-synonym: spectrum"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5494088c-540f-429a-98d2-9e17be5bbace",
                                                "sense_id": "ac90fa31-b945-36bd-8c65-54a883434950",
                                                "text": "So, the white line implies Blacklessness and the black background implies Whitelessness – that is, once the white line, a continuum, has emerged from blackness, also a continuum, and the two continua engage in an “inter-penetrative” (Buddhist term) process."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "093a4633-88f2-49a5-bdc9-1fbb0c83a493",
                                                "sense_id": "ac90fa31-b945-36bd-8c65-54a883434950",
                                                "text": "In fact, the influence of signage in a certain area may exist anywhere on a continuum from profoundly effective to utterly trivial or completely insignificant, irrespective of the intent motivating the signs."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1b43c812-b3d7-366b-9145-ee9f2ad33518",
                                        "entry_id": "2bb1eeb7-75ce-3870-b964-532097bdd2cc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A continuous extent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7fbfefa2-30c5-428e-ab04-781ef4247994",
                                                "sense_id": "1b43c812-b3d7-366b-9145-ee9f2ad33518",
                                                "text": "A doorknob of whatever roundish shape is effectively a continuum of levers, with the axis of the latching mechanism—known as the spindle—being the fulcrum about which the turning takes place."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2a13a801-eec1-39f3-afe5-dc82808712b1",
                                        "entry_id": "2bb1eeb7-75ce-3870-b964-532097bdd2cc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The nondenumerable set of real numbers; more generally, any compact connected metric space."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bc6939b1-f469-38dd-8013-78b8c8b2bb20",
                                        "entry_id": "2bb1eeb7-75ce-3870-b964-532097bdd2cc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A touch-sensitive strip, similar to an electronic standard musical keyboard, except that the note steps are ¹⁄₁₀₀ of a semitone, and so are not separately marked."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c294c277-67c1-4a3e-b8ff-2ccb475d0cb6",
                        "source_entry_id": "96f86e0e-6857-3e23-8d8e-268e37c47536",
                        "source_sense_id": "d040d7c7-4b60-37db-82de-74fe87571bd4",
                        "target_lang_word": "continuum",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "continuum",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a8da514d-e02e-3d55-a69b-58cb245ef2b7",
                                        "entry_id": "8360de50-a8f3-3084-ac31-e213684e0471",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ensemble, espace ou séquence dont les éléments adjacents n’ont pas de différences saillantes et qui est uniquement divisible de manière arbitraire."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Didactique"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "836fcac8-8e96-44df-bf2c-c87f1a123e8b",
                                                "sense_id": "a8da514d-e02e-3d55-a69b-58cb245ef2b7",
                                                "text": "Le cas de l’Afrique subsaharienne est particulièrement intéressant dans la mesure où la diversité des ethnies et l’artificialité des pays issus du découpage colonial établissent un véritable continuum entre migrations nationales et internationales."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "566407ba-c2e7-42d5-a32c-6f86657ae23a",
                                                "sense_id": "a8da514d-e02e-3d55-a69b-58cb245ef2b7",
                                                "text": "Comme exemple de continuum recherche-soin, le programme technologique STxB est emblématique : technologie imaginée à l'Institut Curie, brevets détenus par l'Institut Curie et développement en cours à l'Institut Curie."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0fa99987-b498-472d-916d-ce3c6eb04106",
                                                "sense_id": "a8da514d-e02e-3d55-a69b-58cb245ef2b7",
                                                "text": "Tout cela me donna brièvement le sentiment peut-être pas d’avoir une place dans le monde, il ne faut pas exagérer, mais quand même d’appartenir à une sorte de continuum organique, de regroupement animal."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ca2c2d98-5276-479d-bc69-39d9f463de5f",
                                                "sense_id": "a8da514d-e02e-3d55-a69b-58cb245ef2b7",
                                                "text": "La dichotomie homme-femme n'est pas récente. Or, si l'opposition des sexes semble bien ancrée, la science propose aujourd'hui un nouveau regard : loin de s'opposer, les sexes forment en réalité une espèce de continuum biologique, où toutes les identités sexuelles sont possibles. De quoi redéfinir masculin et féminin."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d8c81dd5-2143-3d99-b272-83677e6b0022",
                                        "entry_id": "8360de50-a8f3-3084-ac31-e213684e0471",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "(1905) Ensemble d’éléments homogènes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "physical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "891810e1-3826-35c2-9187-bf9b0c4560af",
                                        "entry_id": "8360de50-a8f3-3084-ac31-e213684e0471",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "(1935) Continuum espace-temps : espace quadridimensionnel dans la théorie de la relativité générale, dont la quatrième dimension est le temps."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "physical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
